<title>FRANCE: MATIF commodities volume down 16 percent in March.</title>
<headline>MATIF commodities volume down 16 percent in March.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in March fell by 16.0 percent from the previous month and by 21.9 percent compared with March 1996, owners Matif SA said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Detailed figures for commodity contracts were as follows.</p>
<p>			 Volume    Change	Change   Open positions</p>
<p>				     on month    on year   at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts	18,357   -16.0 pct  -21.9 pct    15,012</p>
<p>  Total futures     18,357   -16.0 pct  -19.4 pct    15,012</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>    White sugar ($) 11,942   -24.3 pct  -34.3 pct     8,975</p>
<p>    Potatoes	     360   +42.9 pct  -71.9 pct	 490</p>
<p>    Rapeseed	   4,912   +16.4 pct  +48.2 pct     3,861</p>
<p>    Wheat		1,143   -29.4 pct     N/A	  1,686</p>
<p>  Sugar options	    0					  0</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
